The second series of British reality television series ''[[The Celebrity Traitors]]'' is currently airing on [[BBC One]] since 1 October 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harrison |first=Ellie |date=2026-09-15 |title=''The Celebrity Traitors'' launch date confirmed as BBC drops dramatic new trailer |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-celebrity-traitors-when-start-bbc-b3050631.html |access-date=2026-09-15 |website=[[The Independent]] |language=en |archive-date=15 September 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260915201906/https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-celebrity-traitors-when-start-bbc-b3050631.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Claudia Winkleman]] is presenting the ten-episode series.<ref name="BBC">{{Cite web |last=Lambert |first=Guy |date=2026-05-02 |title=''Celebrity Traitors'' 2026: Full line-up of series two confirmed |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5yx5w43jzko |access-date=2026-05-02 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> The companion show ''[[The Celebrity Traitors: Uncloaked]]'' has also returned, hosted by [[Ed Gamble]].<ref name="bbc-2025">{{Cite web |last=Rufo |first=Yasmin |date=2025-11-10 |title=''Celebrity Traitors'' to return for a second series in 2026 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwy12ln7rnlo |access-date=2026-05-02 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB |archive-date=10 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251110183709/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwy12ln7rnlo |url-status=live }}</ref> The celebrities are competing to win up to £100,000 for their chosen charities.<ref name="BBC" />

==Production==
In November 2025, following the [[The Celebrity Traitors series 1|first series]] (the finale of which was the [[List of most watched television broadcasts in the United Kingdom#Most watched broadcasts by year|most viewed television broadcast]] in the UK in 2025),<ref>{{Cite news |last=Savage |first=Michael |date=2025-11-08 |title=How ''The Celebrity Traitors'' reversed TV's most troubling trend |url=https://www.theguardian.com/news/ng-interactive/2025/nov/08/how-the-celebrity-traitors-reversed-tvs-most-troubling-trend |access-date=2026-05-08 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> it was announced that ''The Celebrity Traitors'' had been renewed for a second series.<ref name="bbc-2025" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Kanter |first=Jake |date=2025-11-10 |title=''The Celebrity Traitors'' Renewed For Second Season By The BBC |url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/the-celebrity-traitors-renewed-season-2-bbc-1236612423/ |access-date=2026-05-02 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]] |language=en-US |archive-date=9 January 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260109062956/https://deadline.com/2025/11/the-celebrity-traitors-renewed-season-2-bbc-1236612423/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Produced by [[Studio Lambert]], the series began filming in May 2026 at [[Ardross, Highland|Ardross Castle]], had concluded by June, and will air later in 2026.<ref name="deadline-may">{{Cite web |last=Kanter |first=Jake |date=2026-05-02 |title=''The Celebrity Traitors'' Season 2 Gathers Cast Including Bella Ramsey |url=https://deadline.com/2026/05/the-celebrity-traitors-full-cast-bella-ramsey-1236878937/ |access-date=2026-05-02 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]] |language=en-US |archive-date=2 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260502133619/https://deadline.com/2026/05/the-celebrity-traitors-full-cast-bella-ramsey-1236878937/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Dorans |first=Charlotte |date=2026-06-04 |title=''Celebrity Traitors'' Richard E Grant reveals "accurate" warning from Celia Imrie |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a71497673/celebrity-traitors-richard-e-grant-celia-imrie/ |access-date=2026-06-07 |website=[[Digital Spy]] |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Jones |first1=Tamera |last2=Weintraub |first2=Steven |date=2026-06-06 |title=''The Celebrity Traitors'' UK Season 2 Is Officially Coming Sooner Than Expected |url=https://collider.com/celebrity-traitors-uk-season-2-richard-e-grant-savage-house-clair-foy-interview/ |access-date=2026-06-07 |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]] |language=en |archive-date=7 June 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260607185047/https://collider.com/celebrity-traitors-uk-season-2-richard-e-grant-savage-house-clair-foy-interview/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Soon after being announced, the celebrities arrived at the nearby [[Inverness Airport]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-05 |title=Inverness Airport staffing issues could affect flights 'for weeks' |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwy275rldr7o |access-date=2026-05-05 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB |archive-date=6 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260506053214/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwy275rldr7o |url-status=live }}</ref> During filming, the cast stayed at the [[Inverness Airport]] [[Courtyard by Marriott]] hotel.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gowans-Eglinton |first=Charlie |date=2026-05-10 |title=What ''Celebrity Traitors'' want on room service: snacks, G&Ts and a chat |url=https://www.thetimes.com/life-style/celebrity/article/celebrity-traitors-room-service-snacks-0wvst9tln |url-access=subscription |access-date=2026-05-11 |website=[[The Times]] |language=en-GB |archive-date=11 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260511083919/https://www.thetimes.com/life-style/celebrity/article/celebrity-traitors-room-service-snacks-0wvst9tln |url-status=live }}</ref>

Prior to the official cast announcement, many celebrities expressed interest in appearing on the show, including [[Amanda Holden]], [[Tom Hiddleston]] and [[Danny Dyer]], who had turned down appearing on the first series. However, none of these celebrities were cast.<ref>{{Cite news |last=McGrath |first=Rachel |date=2026-01-20 |title=All the stars who've put themselves forward for ''Celebrity Traitors'' series 2 |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/celebrity-traitors-series-two-cast-who-b2904130.html |access-date=2026-05-05 |work=[[The Independent]]}}</ref> Despite this, in March 2026 host Claudia Winkleman hinted that "the cast is extraordinary".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Warner |first=Sam |date=2026-03-20 |title=Claudia Winkleman hints that next series of ''Celebrity Traitors'' cast is "extraordinary" |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a70801498/claudia-winkleman-celebrity-traitors-season-2-cast/ |access-date=2026-05-08 |website=[[Digital Spy]] |language=en-GB |archive-date=13 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260513153927/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a70801498/claudia-winkleman-celebrity-traitors-season-2-cast/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

A teaser trailer was released simultaneously with the cast announcement on 2 May 2026, depicting the contestants' names on ''Traitors'' [[slate]]s at an airport; some were misspelt, including "Richardy Grant", "Miranda Heart", and "Rob Bucket" (a reference to the series, in which players often spelt names incorrectly as they voted at the Round Table).<ref name="BBC" /> A first-look trailer featuring the celebrities was released on 27 August 2026.<ref name="deadline-august">{{Cite web |last=Kanter |first=Jake |date=2026-08-27 |title=''The Celebrity Traitors'' Trailer: BBC Promises Season 2 Tears & Shocks |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/the-celebrity-traitors-trailer-bbc-season-2-1237056831/ |access-date=2026-08-27 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]] |language=en-US |archive-date=28 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260828070102/https://deadline.com/2026/08/the-celebrity-traitors-trailer-bbc-season-2-1237056831/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Speaking at the [[Edinburgh International Television Festival|Edinburgh TV Festival]] in August 2026, BBC content chief Kate Phillips said that the series will feature "tears and surprises".<ref name="deadline-august" /> On 5 September, ''[[The Rest Is Entertainment]]'' host [[Richard Osman]] accidentally revealed the series start date as 23 September, but this was incorrect and denied by the BBC.<ref>{{Cite news |author=Press Association |date=2026-09-05 |title=Richard Osman lets slip ''Celebrity Traitors'' season 2 launch date |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/sep/05/richard-osman-lets-slip-celebrity-traitors-season-2-launch-date |access-date=2026-09-06 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> On 15 September, the series was confirmed to begin on 1 October, with episodes airing on Thursdays and Fridays on BBC One at 8pm. A special programme titled ''Traitor or Faithful? Claudia Decides'' was released on [[BBC iPlayer]] after the first episode aired.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cooper-Fiske |first=Casey |date=2026-09-15 |title=Launch date revealed for series two of ''The Celebrity Traitors'' |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/showbiz/celebrity-news/claudia-winkleman-traitors-stephen-fry-bbc-iplayer-bbc-one-b1297097.html |access-date=2026-09-15 |website=[[The Standard (London newspaper)|The Standard]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-09-15 |title=''The Celebrity Traitors'' series 2 air date confirmed and new trailer released |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2026/the-celebrity-traitors-series-2-air-date-trailer/ |access-date=2026-09-15 |website=BBC Media Centre |language=en |archive-date=17 September 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260917101028/https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2026/the-celebrity-traitors-series-2-air-date-trailer/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Contestants==
The 21 celebrities competing in the series were revealed on 2 May 2026.<ref name="deadline-may" /><ref name="independent">{{Cite web |last=Chilton |first=Louis |date=2026-05-02 |title=''Celebrity Traitors'' 2026 confirms star-studded lineup |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/news/celebrity-traitors-2026-lineup-full-james-acaster-b2969381.html |access-date=2026-05-02 |website=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=White |first=Robert |date=2026-05-02 |title=Jerry Hall and Amol Rajan among new ''Celebrity Traitors'' |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2026/05/02/jerry-hall-and-amol-rajan-among-new-celebrity-traitors/ |url-access=subscription |access-date=2026-05-02 |website=[[The Daily Telegraph|The Telegraph]] |archive-date=2 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260502110921/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2026/05/02/jerry-hall-and-amol-rajan-among-new-celebrity-traitors |url-status=live }}</ref> ''[[The Guardian]]'' dubbed the line-up "one of the most high-profile casts ever assembled for a reality TV show".<ref name="guardian">{{Cite news |last=Savage |first=Michael |date=2026-05-09 |title='You don't have to sell them on the idea': how ''Celebrity Traitors'' has seduced the stars |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/may/09/celebrity-traitors-has-seduced-stars |access-date=2026-05-09 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> Significant pre-existing relationships between celebrities include the close friendship of comedians [[Rob Beckett]] and [[Romesh Ranganathan]],<ref name="independent" /><ref name="telegraph">{{Cite web |last=Hogan |first=Michael |date=2026-05-03 |title=This is the ''Celebrity Traitors'' line-up of dreams |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/tv/2026/05/04/who-on-celebrity-traitors-season-two/ |access-date=2026-05-04 |website=[[The Daily Telegraph|The Telegraph]]}}</ref> who have appeared together on ''[[Rob & Romesh Vs]]'',<ref name="BBC" /> Ranganathan and [[Julie Hesmondhalgh]], who are the presenter and narrator respectively on ''[[The Weakest Link (British game show)|The Weakest Link]]''.<ref name="telegraph"/>, while [[Jerry Hall]] and [[Richard E. Grant]] are close friends and neighbours.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mensah |first=Katelyn |date=2026-10-01 |title=''Celebrity Traitors'' boss reacts to Richard E Grant's stunning Traitor reveal |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/reality-tv/celebrity-traitors-richard-e-grant-reveal-newsupdate/ |access-date=2026-10-01 |website=[[Radio Times]] |language=en-GB}}</ref>

