==Reception==
===Critical reception===
Some outlets commented on the lack of sportspeople compared to the previous series, which included [[Tom Daley]], [[Clare Balding]], and finalist [[Joe Marler]].<ref name="guardian" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Smith |first=Patrick |date=2026-05-06 |title=The vital missing ingredient from this year's ''Celebrity Traitors'' cast |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/features/celebrity-traitors-2026-lineup-james-blunt-bella-ramsey-joe-marler-b2971175.html |access-date=2026-05-11 |website=[[The Independent]] |language=en |archive-date=14 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260514225605/https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/features/celebrity-traitors-2026-lineup-james-blunt-bella-ramsey-joe-marler-b2971175.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In September 2026, ''[[The Times]]'' ranked Hesmondhalgh as most likely to win the series.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Glanfield |first1=Tim |last2=Helm |first2=Jake |last3=Jackson |first3=James |date=2026-09-09 |title=Who is going to win ''The Celebrity Traitors''? Every contestant ranked |url=https://www.thetimes.com/culture/tv-radio/article/who-is-going-to-win-the-celebrity-traitors-every-contestant-ranked-jl6l6wvt8 |url-access=subscription |access-date=2026-09-17 |website=[[The Times]]}}</ref>

